# 🚢 Titanic Survival Prediction

An end-to-end Machine Learning project that predicts whether a passenger survived the Titanic disaster using Python, Pandas, Scikit-learn, Logistic Regression, and Flask.

> **This is my first complete Machine Learning pipeline project**, where I worked through the process from data exploration and preprocessing to model training, evaluation, saving the model, and deploying it with Flask.

## 📌 Project Overview

The main goal of this project is to build a Machine Learning model that predicts whether a Titanic passenger survived based on passenger-related information.

This project helped me understand how an ML project works as a complete pipeline rather than just training a model.

The project covers:

* Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)
* Handling missing values
* Categorical data encoding
* Feature selection
* Train-test splitting
* Feature scaling
* Logistic Regression
* Model evaluation
* Cross-validation
* Creating a Machine Learning pipeline
* Saving the trained model using Joblib
* Flask API deployment
* Web-based prediction interface
* Basic model monitoring concepts

---

# 🔄 Complete ML Workflow

The complete workflow followed in this project is:

```text
                 Titanic Dataset
                       │
                       ▼
            Exploratory Data Analysis
                       │
                       ▼
             Check Dataset Structure
              df.head() / df.info()
                       │
                       ▼
             Summary Statistics
                 df.describe()
                       │
                       ▼
              Missing Value Analysis
                       │
                       ▼
              Data Preprocessing
                       │
             ┌─────────┴─────────┐
             ▼                   ▼
       Handle Missing        Remove Unnecessary
          Values                 Features
             │                   │
             └─────────┬─────────┘
                       ▼
             Categorical Encoding
              Sex / Embarked
                       │
                       ▼
              Feature Selection
                       │
                       ▼
               Train-Test Split
                 80% / 20%
                       │
                       ▼
              Feature Scaling
              StandardScaler
                       │
                       ▼
             Logistic Regression
                       │
                       ▼
                Model Training
                       │
                       ▼
              Model Predictions
                       │
                       ▼
             Model Evaluation
                       │
        ┌──────────────┼──────────────┐
        ▼              ▼              ▼
    Accuracy       Precision       Recall
                       │
                       ▼
                   F1-Score
                       │
                       ▼
             5-Fold Cross-Validation
                       │
                       ▼
              Create ML Pipeline
          Scaler + Logistic Regression
                       │
                       ▼
                Save Pipeline
                  Joblib
                       │
                       ▼
               Flask Deployment
                       │
                       ▼
              Web Prediction Page
                       │
                       ▼
                Survival Result
```

---

